{#- The Library, for somebody who has not signed in, and one kind of it (targum-internal#519).

    The shop window a search result lands on. It was one list of 1,315 texts in five
    languages, under a line about Hebrew, with the waitlist at the bottom of all of them.
    Now it stands the catalogue the way the signed-in Library does: Hebrew first, then
    each other language, and inside each the kinds, each with its first rows and a way to
    all of them on a page of its own (`kind_page`), which is this template with one kind.

    It wears the front door's desk (David, 2026-10-24): the bar, the ground, the cards and
    the chrome's face, from `landing.css`, so the public front reads as one place. What is
    the Library's own is in `shelf.css`. No script: every text is a plain link to its own
    page, which is what a crawler follows.

    Expects `shelves` (`_ShelfLanguage`s), `shelf_name`, `total` and `total_n`; a kind's
    page also `kind_page`, `library` and `robots`. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
{{ styles('landing.css', 'shelf.css') }}
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{#- Upright only: nothing on the Library is set in italic. -#}
{{ chrome_face(italic=False) }}
</head>
<body class="landing">
<a class="skip" href="#top">{{ t("landing.page.skip-to-the-page", "Skip to the page") }}</a>
{% with bar_class = 'bar', home = '/', join = '/#join' %}{% include '_front_bar.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}

<main id="top" class="col lib">
  <header class="lib-head">
    {%- if kind_page|default(false) %}
    <a class="lib-back" href="/library"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> {{ library }}</a>
    {%- endif %}
    <h1>{{ shelf_name }}</h1>
    {%- if shelves %}
    <p class="lib-lede">
      {%- if kind_page|default(false) %}{{ tn("shelf.page.texts", total_n, "{count} text", "{count} texts", count=total) }}
      {%- else %}{{ tn("shelf.page.lede", total_n, "{count} text and video to learn from. Every one opens ready to read, with a translation beside it.", "{count} texts and videos to learn from. Every one opens ready to read, with a translation beside it.", count=total) }}{% endif -%}
    </p>
    {%- endif %}
    {#- One line and the one press (§6, §9): the waitlist while the front door takes an
        address, Sign in where it does not. The switch to Sign up comes with #485. -#}
    <p class="lib-ask">
      <span>{{ t("shelf.page.free-to-read-once-you-re-in", "Free to read once you’re in.") }}</span>
      {%- if front_door_is_open() %}
      <a class="btn cta" href="/#join">{{ t("landing.page.join-the-waitlist", "Join the waitlist") }}</a>
      {%- else %}
      <a class="btn cta" href="/account/signin">{{ t("shelf.page.sign-in", "Sign in") }}</a>
      {%- endif %}
    </p>
  </header>

  {%- for shelf in shelves %}
  <section class="lib-lang" id="in-{{ shelf.code }}"{% if not kind_page|default(false) %} aria-labelledby="in-{{ shelf.code }}-head"{% endif %}>
    {%- if not kind_page|default(false) %}
    <h2 id="in-{{ shelf.code }}-head">{{ shelf.name }} <span class="lib-count">· {{ tn("shelf.page.texts", shelf.size, "{count} text", "{count} texts", count=shelf.size) }}</span></h2>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- for kind in shelf.kinds %}
    <section class="lib-kind"{% if not kind_page|default(false) %} aria-labelledby="in-{{ shelf.code }}-{{ kind.kind }}"{% endif %}>
      {%- if not kind_page|default(false) %}
      <div class="lib-kind-head">
        <h3 id="in-{{ shelf.code }}-{{ kind.kind }}">{{ kind.name }}</h3>
        {%- if kind.size > kind.rows|length %}
        <a class="lib-all" href="{{ kind.at }}">{{ t("shelf.page.all", "All {n}", n=kind.size) }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <ul class="texts lib-rows">
        {%- for row in kind.rows %}
        {#- The name, the place and the blurb in the page's language where the catalogue
            has them, the way the text page draws them, and English where it has not
            (targum-internal#520). `lang` says which one is drawn. #}
        {%- set entry = row.entry %}
        {%- set script = entry.language if entry.language in ('arc', 'yi') else 'he' %}
        <li class="lib-row">
          <a href="/library/{{ entry.id }}">
            <bdi class="lib-title" lang="{{ entry.language }}">{{ entry.title }}</bdi>
            {% if row.named %}<span class="english" lang="{{ row.named_lang }}" dir="ltr">{{ row.named }}</span>{% endif %}
          </a>
          {#- A byline or a blurb in Hebrew letters says so, with its own direction
              (design.md §14, line 3; Library QA, 2026-10-20): "אברהם מאפו, 1853" stood in
              an English run. One with a Hebrew word inside a Latin line marks the word
              ("Omid Memarian, תרגם Gallia Hoz"; #477, polish 10). -#}
          <span class="byline"{% if row.byline and 'א' <= row.byline[:1] <= 'ת' %} lang="{{ script }}" dir="auto">{{ row.byline }}{% else %}>{{ row.byline|isolate('ltr', script) }}{% endif %}</span>
          <span class="blurb"{% if row.blurb and 'א' <= row.blurb[:1] <= 'ת' %} lang="{{ script }}" dir="auto">{{ row.blurb }}{% else %}{% if row.blurb and row.blurb_lang != page_language %} lang="{{ row.blurb_lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ row.blurb|isolate('ltr', script) }}{% endif %}</span>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
    {%- endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- else %}
  {#- Said plainly rather than dressed up. An empty shelf that pretends otherwise is
      worse than one that admits it, and this one fills up shortly. -#}
  <p class="empty">{{ t("shelf.page.nothing-here-yet", "Nothing here yet.") }}</p>
  {%- endfor %}
</main>

{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}
</body>
</html>
